From: Fabien Danieau <fabien.danieau@pollen-robotics.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mpph264enc: advertise constrained-baseline

Taken verbatim from patches/gstreamer-rockchip/ in
pollen-robotics/microduck-gst-plugins.

Without it webrtcsink offers no H.264 at all, and mediad restricts video-caps to
H.264, so the result is a producer with no codec: discovery fails with "No caps
found for stream video_0" and every session dies on not-negotiated before a frame
is sent. Observed on this board on 2026-09-15 with the stock plugin, which lists
only { baseline, main, high } -- constrained-baseline is the one profile
webrtcsink's discovery pass demands.

The encoder already produces constrained-baseline-compatible output; the profile
was simply missing from the pad template, so this widens what it will admit to
rather than changing what it does.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/gst/rockchipmpp/gstmpph264enc.c
+++ b/gst/rockchipmpp/gstmpph264enc.c
@@ -98,7 +98,7 @@ GST_STATIC_PAD_TEMPLATE ("src",
         GST_MPP_H264_ENC_SIZE_CAPS ","
         "stream-format = (string) { byte-stream }, "
         "alignment = (string) { au }, "
-        "profile = (string) { baseline, main, high }"));
+        "profile = (string) { constrained-baseline, baseline, main, high }"));

 static GstStaticPadTemplate gst_mpp_h264_enc_sink_template =
 GST_STATIC_PAD_TEMPLATE ("sink",
